  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The diagram shows atomic transitions E<sub>1</sub>, E<sub>2</sub> and E<sub>3</sub> when a particular atom changes its energy state. The wavelengths of the photons that correspond to these transitions are <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{2}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{3}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is correct for these wavelengths?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}&gt;\\lambda_{2}&gt;\\lambda_{3}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}=\\lambda_{2}+\\lambda_{3}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{1}}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{2}+\\lambda_{3}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{1}}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{2}}+\\frac{1}{\\lambda_{3}}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
